From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Relay12 <relay12@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: route Texture2D resources through the On12 backend

Embed the core's Texture2D handle in d3d_texture2d, add the create and
destroy backend operations, and route D3D11 and D3D10 Texture2D creation
through Relay12 for the On12 backend only.  Swapchain-owned textures, which
arrive with a caller-supplied wined3d_texture, stay on the WineD3D path.

A backend texture owns no WineD3D object and no DXGI resource, so every
ID3D11Texture2D and ID3D10Texture2D method that would reach one now tests
for it and reports an honest result instead of dereferencing NULL.

Both backend operation tables also become designated initialisers.  They
were positional, and adding create_texture2d and destroy_texture2d to
struct d3d11_backend_ops shifted every WineD3D entry after destroy_buffer:
destroy_vertex_shader received wined3d_backend_set_vertex_shader, the two
shader binding ops became NULL, and the last two members were left
uninitialised.  That is a defect on the ordinary WineD3D path, not only on
the On12 one, and naming each member prevents the next insertion repeating
it.
